nd justify that the chosen probe is equivalent to today's `diff_cached_names` basename check for the idempotency (HEAD-unmoved) property.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3052,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current site gates commit on `git_adapter.diff_cached_names` = `git diff --cached --name-only` (reconcile_helpers.py:260) after `git_adapter.add`","Plan proposes `git status --porcelain -- <paths>` as the scoped detection probe","`git status --porcelain` and `git diff --cached` are not interchangeable predicates for 'a staged change exists vs HEAD'"],"finding":"The plan silently substitutes the current site's staged-diff change-detection (git diff --cached --name-only, per-file basename check) with `git status --porcelain -- <paths>` in the new helper, but does not reconcile that these two probes differ (porcelain reports working-tree+untracked state; diff --cached reports index-vs-HEAD). The 'per-file idempotency preserved' claim rests on this unproven equivalence.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5f3a063c7b12603d","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (decided) — 'a sequence = git status/add -- <paths> scoped staging'; and Classifications 'Per-file idempotency (bug 1e08) preserved'","norm_id":"ncc3eb8f94644d649","priority":0.2948,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An allowlist file already staged in the index but clean in the working tree","A pass where porcelain reports a delta that produces no index-vs-HEAD diff (or vice versa), moving/not-moving HEAD contrary to the current site's behavior"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Prefer keeping the post-stage `git diff --cached --name-only -- <paths>` gate (matching today's `diff_cached_names`) rather than a pre-stage porcelain probe, so the HEAD-unmoved predicate is byte-for-byte the one the idempotency tests already lock in.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.55,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"